HST Office: the sidebar's frame in the HST look (FrameCoat/Sidebar): tab bar, deck title, panel titles.

- sfx2 sidebar Theme: while the coat and FrameCoat/Sidebar are on and not in high contrast, the tab bar,
  the deck title and the panel titles take the frame surface of the design tokens (Theme::GetHstFrameColor);
  the deck and panel contents and the highlight keep their colours.
- gtk3: tabbar.ui, deck.ui and panel.ui give the frame boxes style classes (hst-sidebar-tabbar,
  hst-sidebar-deck-title, hst-sidebar-panel-title) and vcl/source/hst/coat/css/sidebar.cxx styles them:
  the tab bar's surface and divider towards the deck, its buttons flat until hovered, the open deck on an
  aPill pill (radius::Control) with the accent bar (aSelectedIndicator) along its leading edge, the focus
  mark kept, RTL mirrored; the divider under the deck title and above each panel title; the title bars'
  small buttons flat until hovered. Colours, radii and inset shadows only: no widget changes size.
- VCL backends (Windows, macOS): TabBar paints the surface, the divider and the open deck's accent bar in
  the margin left of its button (Theme::DrawHstTabBarFrame); Deck gives each panel title a tiled
  background of the frame surface with the divider along its top. The tab buttons keep VCL's own look
  until the ribbon's button painter offers a paint-only look (the ribbon's owner-draw also changes the
  button geometry, so it is not used here).
- The deck's name is set in type::Title while the coat is on.
- CppunitTest_sfx2_hst_sidebar_coat: frame keys and content keys, the switches and high contrast, the CSS
  without sizes, the VCL tab bar frame and its indicator.

